<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>Automata-Theory on metafunctor</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/tags/automata-theory/</link><description>Research Engineer &amp; Computer Scientist - Machine Learning, Statistical Computing, Open Source Development</description><language>en-us</language><managingEditor>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</managingEditor><webMaster>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 15:26:07 -0500</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://metafunctor.com/tags/automata-theory/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><image><url>https://metafunctor.com/images/og-image.jpg</url><title>metafunctor</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/</link></image><item><title>Regex Under the Hood</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/post/2022-09-12-regex-machines/</link><pubDate>Mon, 12 Sep 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://metafunctor.com/post/2022-09-12-regex-machines/</guid><description>Your regex compiles into a state machine. Type a pattern, feed it a string, and watch the machine think — step by step.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>You type <code>grep 'a*b+' file.txt</code> and results appear. But what actually happened in that fraction of a second? Your pattern compiled into a <em>state machine</em> — a tiny computer with no memory except &ldquo;where am I right now?&rdquo;</p>
<p>This post builds that machine from scratch and lets you watch it think.</p>
<h2 id="the-pipeline">The Pipeline</h2>
<p>Every regex engine follows the same path:</p>
<p><strong>Regex → NFA → DFA → Match</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Parse</strong> the regex and build a Nondeterministic Finite Automaton (NFA) using Thompson&rsquo;s construction. The NFA can be in <em>multiple states at once</em> and can take free epsilon (ε) transitions without consuming input.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Convert</strong> the NFA to a Deterministic Finite Automaton (DFA) using subset construction. Each DFA state represents a <em>set</em> of NFA states. One state at a time, one transition per symbol.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Simulate</strong> the DFA on input — one character, one lookup, O(n). No backtracking.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="thompsons-construction">Thompson&rsquo;s Construction</h2>
<p>Thompson&rsquo;s construction builds NFAs by snapping together small templates. Each template has exactly one start and one accepting state:</p>
<p><strong>Single character</strong> <code>a</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"><span class="line"><span class="cl">──▶(q0)──a──▶((q1))
</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>Concatenation</strong> <code>ab</code> — chain the fragments, connecting the first&rsquo;s accept to the second&rsquo;s start via ε:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"><span class="line"><span class="cl">──▶(q0)─a─▶(q1)─ε─▶(q2)─b─▶((q3))
</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>Union</strong> <code>a|b</code> — new start fans out via ε, both accepts converge via ε:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"><span class="line"><span class="cl">       ┌─ε─▶(q2)─a─▶(q3)─ε─┐
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">──▶(q0)┤                     ├▶((q5))
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">       └─ε─▶(q4)─b─▶(q5)─ε─┘
</span></span></code></pre></div><p><strong>Kleene star</strong> <code>a*</code> — ε-bypass for zero occurrences, ε-loop for repetition:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"><span class="line"><span class="cl">    ┌────────ε────────┐
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">    │   ┌──ε──┐       │
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">──▶(q0)─ε─▶(q1)─a─▶(q2)─ε─▶((q3))
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">    │                       ▲
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">    └───────────ε───────────┘
</span></span></code></pre></div><p>These compose mechanically. <code>(a|b)*abb</code> nests a union inside a star, then concatenates three symbols. The result is a graph of states and transitions that <em>exactly</em> encodes the regex&rsquo;s meaning.</p>
<h2 id="try-it">Try It</h2>
<p>Type a regex and an input string. <strong>Build</strong> constructs the NFA, then <strong>Step</strong> through the input one character at a time. Watch which states light up — the NFA explores all possibilities simultaneously.</p>
<div id="nfa-sim">
  <div class="sim-controls">
    <div class="sim-fields">
      <div class="sim-field">
        <label for="sim-regex">Pattern</label>
        <input id="sim-regex" type="text" value="(a|b)*abb" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <div class="sim-field">
        <label for="sim-input">Input</label>
        <input id="sim-input" type="text" value="aabb" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <button id="sim-build">Build</button>
    </div>
    <div class="sim-presets">
      <button data-regex="(a|b)*abb" data-input="aabb">classic</button>
      <button data-regex="a*b+" data-input="aaabb">a*b+</button>
      <button data-regex="(ab|cd)*" data-input="ababcd">groups</button>
      <button data-regex="a(b|c)*d" data-input="abcbd">nested</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sim-error" id="sim-error"></div>
  <div class="sim-tabs">
    <button class="sim-tab active" data-tab="nfa">NFA</button>
    <button class="sim-tab" data-tab="dfa">DFA</button>
  </div>
  <div class="sim-canvas">
    <svg id="sim-svg"></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="sim-legend" id="sim-legend"></div>
  <div class="sim-tape" id="sim-tape"></div>
  <div class="sim-playback">
    <button id="sim-reset" disabled>Reset</button>
    <button id="sim-step" disabled>Step</button>
    <button id="sim-play" disabled>Play</button>
  </div>
  <div class="sim-result" id="sim-result"></div>
  <div class="sim-trace" id="sim-trace"></div>
</div>
